title: 'pallet-balances: scope `ReservableCurrency` operations to their own reserves'

doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    `pallet-balances` tracks holds and named reserves in their own storage, while the unnamed
    reserves are whatever remains of an account's reserved balance. The unnamed
    `ReservableCurrency` operations (`unreserve`, `slash_reserved` and `repatriate_reserved`) and
    the `force_unreserve` call now act on that remainder only, and the `NamedReservableCurrency`
    operations act on their own named reserve only.

    Callers that only release, slash or move what they have reserved themselves see no change.

    A new Root-only `force_unreserve_named` call is the named counterpart of `force_unreserve`.

crates:
- name: pallet-balances
  bump: major
- name: pallet-preimage
  bump: none
